          1.05
        ]
      },
      "frases": [
        {
          "es": "Su nombre, Hades, significa «el que no se ve». Muy pocos vieron alguna vez su cara.",
          "en": "His name, Hades, means “the unseen one”. Very few ever saw his face."
        },
        {
          "es": "Los Cíclopes, herreros gigantes de un solo ojo, le hicieron un regalo: un casco que lo volvía invisible.",
          "en": "The Cyclopes, giant smiths with one eye, made him a gift: a helmet that made him invisible."
        },
        {
          "es": "También era el señor de las riquezas, porque el oro, la plata y las semillas salen de debajo de la tierra.",
          "en": "He was also the lord of riches, because gold, silver and seeds all come from under the ground."
        },
        {
          "es": "La gente tenía miedo de decir su nombre. En su lugar, lo llamaban Plutón, «el rico».",
          "en": "People were afraid to say his name. Instead, they called him Pluto, “the rich one”."
        },
        {
          "es": "Hades no era malvado. Era estricto. En su reino, los muertos entraban, y nadie salía.",
          "en": "Hades was not evil. He was strict. In his kingdom, the dead came in, and no one went out."
        }
      ],
