        "zoom": [
          1,
          1.06
        ]
      },
      "frases": [
        {
          "es": "Por fin, Orfeo llegó ante Hades y su reina, Perséfone.",
          "en": "At last, Orpheus stood before Hades and his queen, Persephone."
        },
        {
          "es": "Cantó sobre su amor, y sobre el día en que la perdió. Pidió una sola cosa: que se la devolvieran.",
          "en": "He sang about his love, and about the day he lost her. He asked for only one thing: give her back."
        },
        {
          "es": "Ovidio cuenta que, por primera vez, las Furias lloraron. Eran los feroces espíritus de la venganza.",
          "en": "Ovid says that, for the first time ever, the Furies cried. They were the fierce spirits of revenge."
        },
        {
          "es": "Hades y Perséfone no pudieron negarse. Llamaron a Eurídice.",
          "en": "Hades and Persephone could not say no. They called for Eurydice."
        },
        {
          "es": "Ella salió despacio de entre las sombras recién llegadas, todavía cojeando por su herida.",
          "en": "She came slowly out from among the new shades, still limping from her wound."
        }
      ],
